  "notes": "Adams County Republicans elect committee members in odd-year municipal primaries for 4-year terms, and the number of seats varies by election district (1 to 12; 331 total) under the party's by-laws, so seats_per_precinct is null and seats are labelled Member 1..N. The 2026 Republican primary ballot has no county committee contest and the 2024 primary results have none either. Seat status: for each district with N seats, seats up to the number of ballot candidates who received votes are filled; any remaining seats are unknown where write-in votes were cast (true in every district with open seats) and would be empty only if no write-in votes were cast. The county published a separate scanned list of Republican committee write-in winners and tie draws (see sources); it was not machine-read here, so those seats stay unknown pending manual review, and write-in winners may also have declined. The precinct report used is labelled UNOFFICIAL; it is the only 2025 primary precinct report on the county's archive page. Appointments since May 2025 are not captured."
